    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can customize the style of the automatic cross reference text using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "xrefstyle"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attribute. This customization brings the cross reference text formatting from the DocBook toolchain to AsciiDoc processing, specifically during conversion."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Since this is a newer feature of the AsciiDoc language, it may not be supported by all converters. Where you can find support for it is in Asciidoctor’s HTML, PDF, and EPUB 3 converters. It’s not supported by the DocBook converter since it’s a feature the DocBook toolchain already provides."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "caution"
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, the cross reference text matches the title of the referenced element. For example, if you’re linking to a section titled “Installation”, the text of the cross reference link appears as:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Installation"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the reftext attribute is specified on the referenced element, that value is preferred over its title. For example, let’s assume the section from the previous example was written as:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[reftext=\"Installation Procedure\"]\n=== Installation"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In this case, the text of the cross reference link appears as:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Installation Procedure"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Attribute references are substituted in the reftext during parsing and reftext substitutions (specialchars, quotes, and replacements) are applied to the value when it’s used during conversion."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the reftext is not specified, the text of the cross reference is automatically generated. By default, this text is the title of the reference."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_default_styling",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Default styling"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The generated text of a cross reference is controlled by the xrefstyle. It will also vary for different element types (section, figure, etc). Let’s consider the following document to learn how the xrefstyle value affects the generated text of a cross reference."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "== Installation\n\n.Big Cats\nimage::big-cats.png[]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "There are three built-in styles supported by the xrefstyle document attribute that you can choose from to customize the generated text of a cross reference."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Uses the signifier for the reference followed by the reference number and emphasized (chapter or appendix) or title enclosed in quotes (e.g., Section 2.3, “Installation”) (e.g., Figure 1, “Big Cats”)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": ":xrefstyle: full"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Uses the signifier for the reference followed by the reference number (e.g., Section 2.3) (e.g., Figure 1)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": ":xrefstyle: short"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Uses the title only, only applying emphasis if the reference is a chapter or appendix (e.g., Installation) (e.g., Big Cats)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": ":xrefstyle: basic"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "xrefstyle"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute can also be specified directly on the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "xref macro"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "xref.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to override the xrefstyle value for a single reference (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "xref:installation[xrefstyle=short]"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). The element attribute supports the same three styles."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The xrefstyle formatting only applies to references that have both a title and number (or explicit caption), but no explicit reftext. If the reference is a chapter or an appendix, the title is displayed in italics instead of quotes (even when the xrefstyle is basic)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s assume you want to reference a section titled “Installation” that has the number 2.3. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "full"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " style is displayed as:"
              }
            ],
